14	/// The single `create()`/`retry()` entry point for all three capture
15	/// cubits (`TextEntryCubit`/`AudioEntryCubit`/`PhotoEntryCubit`) — Intent:
16	/// "the tracker, not `MeusRegistrosCubit`, owns reconciliation". Pure
17	/// Dart, no `package:flutter`/`data` import (RNF06) — a port+impl pair in
18	/// one file, same structural convention `SessionExpiryNotifier`/
19	/// `SessionExpiryNotifierImpl` already use.
20	abstract class PendingEntryWriteTracker {
21	  /// Identical contract to [EntriesRepository.create] (Boundaries) — every
22	  /// capture cubit swaps its `EntriesRepository` dependency for this one,
23	  /// with no other call-site change. Internally: records an optimistic
24	  /// [PendingEntryWrite] (status [PendingEntryWriteInFlight]) *before*
25	  /// calling through to the repository, so [pendingWrites] reflects it
26	  /// immediately; on success, drops the record and emits the confirmed
27	  /// [Entry] on [confirmedWrites]; on failure, flips the record to
28	  /// [PendingEntryWriteFailed] and leaves it for [retry].
29	  Future<Either<Failure, Entry>> create({
30	    required String content,
31	    required EntrySource source,
32	    int? mediaDurationSeconds,
33	  });
34	
35	  /// Replays the exact same payload a failed write ([tempId]) was created
36	  /// with (Never: "a second retry endpoint — retry replays `create()`
37	  /// verbatim"). A no-op for an unknown [tempId] or one that isn't
38	  /// currently [PendingEntryWriteFailed] (e.g. already in flight, or
39	  /// already resolved).
40	  Future<void> retry(String tempId);
41	
42	  /// Releases the underlying stream resources — wired into `get_it`'s own
43	  /// reset lifecycle (`entries_injection.dart`'s `dispose:`), same
44	  /// convention `SessionExpiryNotifier.dispose()`/`SessionRepository.
45	  /// dispose()` already use.
46	  Future<void> dispose();
47	
48	  /// Every write this tracker currently holds (in flight or failed) —
49	  /// `MeusRegistrosCubit` overlays this on its own confirmed list (Intent).
50	  /// Replay-capable: a late subscriber sees the current snapshot
51	  /// immediately rather than only future changes (`Stream.multi` + cached
52	  /// last value, mirrors `SessionRepositoryImpl.statusStream`,
53	  /// `session_repository_impl.dart:69-89`) — necessary here because
54	  /// `MeusRegistrosCubit` is a long-lived singleton that may subscribe
55	  /// well after a write is already pending (e.g. the user opens "Meus
56	  /// Registros" after already starting a save from Home).
57	  Stream<List<PendingEntryWrite>> get pendingWrites;
58	
59	  /// Broadcasts the real, server-confirmed [Entry] — paired with the
60	  /// [PendingEntryWrite.tempId] it resolved from — the instant a
61	  /// [create]/[retry] call resolves successfully. The one channel
62	  /// `MeusRegistrosCubit` (which never calls [create]/[retry] itself, and
63	  /// never talks to a capture cubit directly, AD-7) has to learn of a
64	  /// just-confirmed write and prepend it into its own state (Boundaries:
65	  /// "tracker drops the record; `MeusRegistrosCubit` prepends the
66	  /// confirmed `Entry` into its own state"). No replay semantics, same
67	  /// rationale `SessionExpiryNotifier.expiredEvents` already documents: a
68	  /// one-shot signal per confirmation, not a value a late subscriber needs
69	  /// to catch up on — a write that confirmed before `MeusRegistrosCubit`
70	  /// ever subscribed will simply arrive through its next `list()`
71	  /// instead.
72	  ///
73	  /// The paired `tempId` (Review finding) lets a listener drop its own
74	  /// locally-held pending placeholder for this exact write in the very
75	  /// same synchronous handler that prepends the confirmed [Entry] —
76	  /// `pendingWrites`' own removal of the same record is a separate
77	  /// `Stream.multi`-wrapped subscription that can otherwise deliver one
78	  /// microtask late, which previously left a one-frame window where both
79	  /// the stale placeholder and the real confirmed entry rendered at once.
80	  Stream<({String tempId, Entry entry})> get confirmedWrites;
81	}
